  body: "# Assessment period for JSA and IS self-employment\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source
    bases normal weekly self-employed earnings on receipts and expenses paid during an assessment period,
    with period selection responsive to a new business or a change in normal trading.\n\n## Scope and
    exceptions\n\nDo not assume the previous tax year or a universal twelve-month period. Stable established
    businesses, newer businesses and changes have separate provisions; royalties and similar payments
    also differ. Source examples illustrate the guidance and are not current entitlements. No cash-flow
    or profit calculation is implemented.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 27051, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n- [DMG 27052, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n- [DMG 27060, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n- [DMG 27062, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\n\
    Model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch27`: PDF SHA-256 `90b6c5ec739d2366936d67d78cd5a6f857b764b92000200f4a44ac956c88b3ac`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `7f84279f4a44373405ce06d32bf1c927a9f25dda507895b1540e6bb8b1b5185a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-business-expense-conditions
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Receipts and paid expenses are the stated inputs; the expense provision separately
      requires payment during that assessment period and other conditions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0014
      quote: "27051 The normal weekly earnings of a S/E earner should be calculated by using the\n\n\n\
        1. gross receipts (see DMG 27125) and\n\n\n2. expenses paid out (see DMG 27190)\n\n\nduring the
        assessment period. Different rules apply for royalties, copyright payments and Public Lending\n\
        Rights payments."
      locator: DMG 27051
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0034
      quote: "27190 When calculating the net profit of a S/E earner the DM should deduct from the gross
        receipts any\n\nbusiness expense that1\n\n\n1. was paid out wholly and exclusively for the purposes
        of the business 2 and\n\n\n2. was paid out during the assessment period and\n\n\n3. was reasonably
        incurred3 (see DMG 27198) and\n\n\n4. is an allowable expense (see DMG 27206).\n\n\n         \
        \                   1 JSA Regs, reg 101(4)(a); IS (Gen) Regs, reg 38(3)(a); 2 JSA Regs, reg 101(9)(a);\n\
        \                               IS (Gen) Regs, reg 38(8)(a); 3 JSA Regs, reg 101(8); IS (Gen)
        Regs, reg 38(7)"
      locator: DMG 27190
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The changing-period procedure expressly refers to supersession if new figures affect
      entitlement and distinguishes a decision not to supersede.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0015
      quote: "27062 The earnings would then be averaged over that period and apportioned on a weekly basis
        until\nthe figures for the following week or month become available. The assessment period would
        then be\nextended. The assessment period would\n\n\n1. start on the date the change affecting
        the pattern of business occurred and\n\n\n2. end on the date that the new figures became available.\n\
        \n\nThe DM should supersede if the new figures affect entitlement to IS or JSA. Where entitlement
        is not\naffected, a decision not to supersede should be made if the claimant asked for earnings
        to be looked at\nagain. For further guidance on supersession including the effective date rule,
        see DMG Chapter 04."
      locator: DMG 27062
